# AI Shelf flow definitions

When the user asks to create or edit an automation flow for AI Shelf, output a **`.flow.md`** file.

## File format

- YAML frontmatter + Markdown body (the body is the Claude agent prompt when `runner: claude`).
- Save under `%APPDATA%/ai-shelf/flows/{id}.flow.md` (or project `flows/` folder).

## Required frontmatter

```yaml
---
schema: ai-shelf.flow/definition/v1
id: my-flow-id
enabled: true
timeout_sec: 600
phases:
  - id: step-one
    label: Short human label
  - id: step-two
    label: Another step
---
```

## Optional frontmatter

```yaml
schedule: "0 9 * * 1-5"   # cron, Asia/Taipei unless timezone set
timezone: Asia/Taipei
runner: claude            # default | http for simple checks
url: https://example.com  # when runner: http
method: HEAD
on_fail: slack            # requires AISHELF_FLOW_SLACK_WEBHOOK
output: ~/reports/{id}-{date}.md
```

## Claude runner protocol

The body must instruct the agent to report progress with stdout lines:

```
FLOW_PROGRESS {"type":"phase.started","phaseId":"step-one"}
FLOW_PROGRESS {"type":"phase.done","phaseId":"step-one","message":"optional"}
```

Mark each major step in the body with a heading that includes the phase id:

```markdown
## 【step-one】Gather data

...
```

End output after the line `FLOW_OUTPUT_BEGIN` (the runner captures everything after as `output.md`).

## HTTP runner

For connectivity or simple API checks without Claude:

```yaml
runner: http
url: https://www.google.com
method: HEAD
phases:
  - id: check
    label: HTTP check
```

## Examples

- Daily report: `schedule: "0 8 * * *"`, multiple phases, `on_fail: slack`
- Weekly cleanup: `schedule: "0 3 * * 0"`
- Manual only: omit `schedule`

Do not invent n8n-style nodes. One markdown file = one DAG defined by `phases` order.
